    test(validate): run every lane suite and report SKIPPED for missing logs (Issue #83)
    
    run_suite_lane returned 1 on the first failing suite, so every suite
    ordered after it in that lane never ran and never left a log. Under
    set -e the ordered cat replay then died on the first missing log: one
    FAILED line, a truncated replay that even hid logs which did exist, and
    a bare "cat: ... No such file or directory" instead of a list of
    untested suites.
    
    The lane now accumulates a status and runs every suite, so each failure
    still prints FAILED and the lane exits nonzero after all suites are
    measured. The replay cats every log that exists and prints an explicit
    SKIPPED for any suite that left none, marking the run nonzero rather
    than aborting on a cat error. Green-path output is unchanged.
    
    test-issue-83-lane-failure-visibility.py extracts the real lane/replay
    block and drives stub suites through it: a failure does not hide
    downstream suites, a missing log is reported SKIPPED with a nonzero
    exit, and the green path passes.
    
